<title>UK: Euromarket turnover rose in week to 24 July  -ISMA.</title>
<headline>Euromarket turnover rose in week to 24 July  -ISMA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in the Eurobond and related markets rose to $1.073 trillion in the week to July 24 from $1.019 trillion in the previous week, International Securities Market Association figures show (in billions of dollars).</p>
<p>					    LATEST WEEK	PREVIOUS WEEK</p>
<p> PRIMARY MARKET:			   48.47		     59.98</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	  27.84		     30.61</p>
<p> SECONDARY MARKET:		     1025.50		    977.16</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	 748.37		    264.16</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH EUROCLEAR	    771.18		    737.18</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH CEDEL		  302.15		    299.89</p>
<p>--London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
